{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>You shall keep My Sabbaths.</b> Even during the days of subjugation, even though the rest upon them is a remembrance of freedom." "<b>And you shall revere My sanctuary.</b> The places consecrated in exile — the synagogues and study halls — even though the Temple was destroyed, as it says: וָאֱהִי לָהֶם לְמִקְדָּשׁ מְעָט (Ezekiel 11:16), and the Sages of blessed memory said (Megillah 29a): these are the synagogues and study halls."], :book :leviticus, :voice :sforno, :lang :en, :chapter 26, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-22T16:38:06.731274854Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}